 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The Spam can is exactly the right shape.</li><li>Wash it, line it with plastic wrap so the rice lifts out, and mind the edges if it was opened with a can opener.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Can as the mold"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Mirin and sugar caramelise fast.</li><li>As soon as the sauce turns thick and shiny, get the slices out of the pan.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Don't burn the glaze"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Best the same day, at room temperature.</li><li>Wrapped tightly in plastic wrap they keep a few hours; the fridge hardens the rice.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Keeping"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The egg layer (Spam-and-egg musubi, a common Hawaii version) is this site's addition.</li><li>The oil and the narrow nori strips (a belt with the Spam showing at both ends) follow Christie at Home; The Heirloom Pantry uses half sheets that wrap the whole block.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Added here"
  }
 ],
